Node tracing (border cycle for polygon fill): BFS or DFS: [BFS],[explored,frontier,unseen]

- may be possible to have "two softbodies in one" with this approach
- in a cycle, every node touches 2 other nodes.
- border nodes may form 2 connected components through node adjacency
- this way, does not depend on node ID 

algorithm pseudocode: 
for each BORDER NODE:
    find how many connected components exist (n number)

    OR

while border nodes copy is not empty

for n times: (does not run if n=0)
    find a node in one unique/untouched connected component (remove that node from list, so that after 1 iteration, all nodes from that sub-graph are gone from the list)
    trace
    end current iteration when end node == start node